{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Sustain your hearts.</b> In the Torah, in the Prophets, and in the Writings we find that bread is the sustenance of the heart. In the Torah: ״וְסַעֲדוּ לִבְּכֶם״. In the Prophets: ״סְעָד לִבְּךָ פַּת לֶחֶם״ (Judges 19). In the Writings: ״וְלֶחֶם לְבַב אֱנוֹשׁ יִסְעָד״ (Psalms 104). Rabbi Chama said: it is not written לְבַבְכֶם here but לִבְּכֶם — this teaches that the evil inclination has no dominion over the angels (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>Afterward you may pass on.</b> Afterward you shall go." "<b>For on this account you have passed by.</b> For this thing is what I ask of you, since you have passed by to do me honor." "<b>For on this account.</b> Like עַל אֲשֶׁר. And so every כִּי עַל כֵּן in Scripture: ״כִּי עַל כֵּן בָּאוּ בְּצֵל קֹרָתִי״ (Genesis 19), ״כִּי עַל כֵּן רָאִיתִי פָנֶיךָ״ (Genesis 33:10), ״כִּי עַל כֵּן לֹא נְתַתִּיהָ״ (ibid. 38), ״כִּי עַל כֵּן יָדַעְתָּ חֲנֹתֵנוּ״ (Numbers 10)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:12.478442939Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}